    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Lake Chad empire ruled for close to eight centuries by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sayfawa-dynasty">Sayfawa dynasty</a>, one of the longest in world history.</li><li>Its control of the trans-Saharan route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#tripoli">Tripoli</a> and its Islamic institutions tied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#central-sudan">central Sudan</a> to the Muslim world.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#fulani-war">Fulani jihad</a>, the rise of the shehus and Rabih's 1893 conquest ended it before European powers divided the land.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>As early as the thirteenth century, a hostel for students and pilgrims from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-kanem">Kanem</a> was maintained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cairo">Cairo</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

